IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca03-types`

-- Communications Act 2003 (UK) — THE THREE GOALS.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2003-21.txt.

§ `Rules`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `Goal 1 — ending a contract early (ss 124U-124V)`

-- s 51(9)(a)-(c): a qualifying end-user.
@ref s 51(9)
GIVEN e IS A `End-user`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying end-user` e IF
    NOT (e EQUALS `another end-user`)

-- s 124U(1), (3): the section applies where the end-user has a right to
-- terminate early; for a machine-to-machine service, only for a qualifying
-- end-user.
@ref s 124U(1), (3)
GIVEN t IS A `Early termination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 124U applies to` t IF
        t's `I have a right to terminate early`
    AND ((NOT (t's `a machine-to-machine service`)) OR `a qualifying end-user` (t's `who I am`))

-- s 124U(1)(a)-(b), (2): "no compensation is to be due by the end-user,
-- except compensation for any retained terminal equipment", not exceeding
-- "the lesser of— (a) the remaining part of any fee for the service until
-- the end of the agreed contract period; or (b) a proportion of the value of
-- the terminal equipment, as agreed ..., corresponding to the proportion of
-- the agreed contract period that remains unexpired."
@ref s 124U(1)-(3)
@export The most I can be made to pay for ending my phone or broadband contract early, under s 124U of the Communications Act 2003 (UK): nothing except compensation for terminal equipment I keep, and that no more than the lesser of the remaining fees to the end of the agreed period and the unexpired share of the equipment's agreed value. NOTHING where s 124U does not apply. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Early termination`  @desc The right to terminate, who I am, the service, the equipment and the fees
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most I can be made to pay for ending early` t MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 124U applies to` t)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF t's `I keep the terminal equipment`
         THEN JUST (`the lesser of` (t's `remaining fees to the end of the period`) `and` share)
         ELSE JUST 0
    WHERE
        share MEANS t's `agreed value of the equipment` TIMES t's `unexpired months` DIVIDED BY t's `agreed contract months`

-- s 124U(4): for a bundled contract, s 124U(1) applies to all its elements
-- unless the end-user is a small business or small not-for-profit body and
-- has waived the rights.
@ref s 124U(4)
@export Do my rights on ending early cover every element of my bundled contract, under s 124U(4) of the Communications Act 2003 (UK)? Yes, unless I am a small business or small not-for-profit body that has waived them. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Early termination`  @desc The contract, who I am and any waiver
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my rights cover the whole bundle for` t IF
        `s 124U applies to` t
    AND t's `a bundled contract`
    AND NOT (    (t's `who I am` EQUALS `a business with no more than 10 workers`
                  OR t's `who I am` EQUALS `a not-for-profit body with no more than 10 workers`)
             AND t's `I waived the bundle rights`)

-- s 124V: an individual not acting for a business, with a right to end an
-- element of a bundled contract early for lack of conformity or failure to
-- supply, may end all of its elements.
@ref s 124V
@export May I end every element of my bundled contract because one element did not conform or was not supplied, under s 124V of the Communications Act 2003 (UK)? Yes, if I am an individual not acting for a business and that failure gave me a right to end that element early. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Early termination`  @desc The contract, who I am, and the failure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I may end the whole bundle for` t IF
        t's `who I am` EQUALS `an individual not acting for a business`
    AND t's `a bundled contract`
    AND t's `I have a right to terminate early`
    AND t's `an element did not conform or was not supplied`

§§ `Goal 2 — TV licensing (ss 363-368)`

-- s 363(1)-(2), (5)-(6), 368(3)
@ref ss 363(1)-(2), (5)-(6), 368(3)
@export Would I commit an offence under s 363 of the Communications Act 2003 (UK) by installing or using a television receiver? Yes if I install or use it to receive television programmes or BBC on-demand programmes without a TV licence covering it, unless only for a dealer's purposes on delivery, demonstration, testing or repair, or exempt by regulations. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN v IS A `TV case`  @desc What I install or use, any licence, and any dealer purpose or exemption
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I would commit a TV licence offence for` v IF
        v's `I install or use a receiver for TV or BBC on-demand`
    AND NOT (v's `I hold a TV licence covering it`)
    AND NOT (v's `only for a dealer's purposes`)
    AND NOT (v's `exempt by regulations`)

-- A person attains an age on the anniversary of birth; 29 February falls on
-- 28 February in a common year (F4).
GIVEN b IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `born on` b `is at least` n `on` d IF
    `add months` b (12 TIMES n) AT MOST d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the month of` d MEANS
    `the day before` (`add months` (Date 1 (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d)) 1)

-- s 365A(2): the age "must be 65 or higher, at or before the end of the
-- month in which the licence is issued".
@ref s 365A(2)
@export Do I meet the age requirement of a TV licence concession under s 365A(2) of the Communications Act 2003 (UK)? Yes if I am of or above the concession's specified age at or before the end of the month the licence is issued. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN k IS A `Concession case`  @desc My date of birth, the day the licence is issued, and the concession's age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I meet the concession's age for` k IF
    `born on` (k's `born on`) `is at least` (k's `specified age`) `on` (`the end of the month of` (k's `licence issued on`))

@ref s 365A(2)
@export Is the concession's age one the BBC may set under s 365A(2) of the Communications Act 2003 (UK)? Only 65 or higher. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN k IS A `Concession case`  @desc The concession's age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the concession's age is allowed for` k IF
    k's `specified age` AT LEAST 65

-- s 366(4): no entry "at any time more than one month after the day on
-- which the warrant was granted".
@ref s 366(4)
@export The last day a TV licensing search warrant can be used to enter, under s 366(4) of the Communications Act 2003 (UK): one month after the day it was granted (the corresponding date, or the last day of the month where there is none). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN g IS A DATE  @desc The day the warrant was granted
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the warrant can be used, granted on` g MEANS `add months` g 1

§§ `Goal 3 — misuse of a network (ss 127-130)`

@ref s 127(1)-(2), (4)
@export Is what I did an offence under s 127 of the Communications Act 2003 (UK)? Yes if I sent (or caused to be sent) over a public electronic communications network a grossly offensive, indecent, obscene or menacing message, or, to cause annoyance, inconvenience or needless anxiety, a message I knew to be false or persistent use of the network; not in the course of providing a programme service. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN m IS A `Message case`  @desc What I sent and why, and whether in a programme service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an offence under s 127 for` m IF
        (   m's `grossly offensive, indecent, obscene or menacing`
         OR m's `a message I knew to be false, to annoy`
         OR m's `persistent use, to annoy`)
    AND NOT (m's `in the course of providing a programme service`)

-- s 127(5): both "(a) before the end of the period of 3 years beginning
-- with the day on which the offence was committed, and (b) before the end of
-- the period of 6 months beginning with the day on which evidence comes to
-- the knowledge of the prosecutor".
@ref s 127(5)
@export The last day an information for a s 127 offence may be laid in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, under s 127(5) of the Communications Act 2003 (UK): the earlier of the end of the 3 years beginning with the day of the offence and the end of the 6 months beginning with the day the prosecutor had sufficient evidence. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN m IS A `Message case`  @desc The day of the offence and the day the prosecutor had sufficient evidence
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to prosecute for` m MEANS
    `the earlier of` (`the last day of the` 36 `months beginning with` (m's `offence on`))
                     (`the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` (m's `evidence known to the prosecutor on`))

@ref s 127(5)
GIVEN m IS A `Message case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prosecution is in time for` m IF
    m's `information laid on` AT MOST `the last day to prosecute for` m

-- s 128(3): the representation period "must not be less than ... (a) in an
-- urgent case, seven days; and (b) in any other case, one month".
@ref s 128(3)-(4)
@export The earliest day Ofcom's period for my representations on a notification of persistent misuse may end, under s 128(3) of the Communications Act 2003 (UK): seven days after the notification in an urgent case, otherwise one month after it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Misuse notification`  @desc The day of the notification and whether Ofcom consider it urgent
GIVETH A DATE
`the shortest representation period ends on` n MEANS
    IF n's `an urgent case`
    THEN `the day` 7 `days after` (n's `notified on`)
    ELSE `add months` (n's `notified on`) 1

@ref s 128(3)
GIVEN n IS A `Misuse notification`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the representation period is long enough for` n IF
    n's `representations allowed until` AT LEAST `the shortest representation period ends on` n

-- ss 129(1)(b)-(c), 130(1)(b)-(c): Ofcom may give an enforcement
-- notification or impose a penalty only once the period has expired.
@ref ss 129(1), 130(1)
@export May Ofcom give me an enforcement notification or impose a penalty for persistent misuse on the day it acts, under ss 129(1) and 130(1) of the Communications Act 2003 (UK)? Only after the period for my representations has expired, and that period must have been long enough under s 128(3). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Misuse notification`  @desc The notification, the period given and the day Ofcom act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Ofcom may act on the day for` n IF
        `the representation period is long enough for` n
    AND n's `Ofcom act on` GREATER THAN n's `representations allowed until`

@ref s 130(4)
@export Is the penalty for persistent misuse within the maximum of £2,000,000 under s 130(4) of the Communications Act 2003 (UK)? DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A `Misuse notification`  @desc The penalty
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the penalty is within the maximum for` n IF
    n's `penalty` AT MOST 2000000
